No. No mines, no quest, no 'side levels' at all. The dungeon is 3.0 was
strictly 'linear' with some special levels.

>3) Spellbooks appear to vanish after a single reading. Do you have to
>relearn spells after some uses or is the incantation known forever?
>(barring an encounter with Maud, of course.)

The 3.0 spell system was barely useful. So no way - you have to find a new
spellbook.

>4) Any other general advice? Mainly, are there things one commonly does
>in 3.1.3 which are a no-no in 3.0j?

Probably not... There are thing that you'll not be able to do, or you may
expect to work slightly differently, but probably none of them disastrous.
Big differences are that monsters don't use items (so you may leave junk
laying around without problems) and relative importance of some items changes.
Ah, almost forgot: you need fire resistance to enter hell, without it
you are fried. And: hell had no down staircases in 3.0 - only up...

